  "mymemory:Currently this front end allows the configuration to the Dropbear port 22 on the box only - any other connections must be configured by yourself - this application allows wrong configurations too easily. Please note that with this tunnel the Dropbear SSH daemon is freely reachable from the Internet if you don't configure a pre-shared key. This tunnel can be used to establish a SOCKSv5 connection to your box when using the OpenSSH client on your source host. Use the following commands as normal user on your source host (the first establishes the dns2tcp tunnel listening on port 2222, the second establishes the SOCKSv5 tunnel listening on port 1080) - the name dns2tcp.meine.domain has to be replaced with the name configured above:<br><pre>dns2tcpc -r ssh -l 2222 -k preshared_key -z dns2tcp.meine.domain dns_server_ip<br>ssh root@localhost -p 2222 -D 1080<br></pre>": {
    "original": "Currently this front end allows the configuration to the Dropbear port 22 on the box only - any other connections must be configured by yourself - this application allows wrong configurations too easily. Please note that with this tunnel the Dropbear SSH daemon is freely reachable from the Internet if you don't configure a pre-shared key. This tunnel can be used to establish a SOCKSv5 connection to your box when using the OpenSSH client on your source host. Use the following commands as normal user on your source host (the first establishes the dns2tcp tunnel listening on port 2222, the second establishes the SOCKSv5 tunnel listening on port 1080) - the name dns2tcp.meine.domain has to be replaced with the name configured above:<br><pre>dns2tcpc -r ssh -l 2222 -k preshared_key -z dns2tcp.meine.domain dns_server_ip<br>ssh root@localhost -p 2222 -D 1080<br></pre>",
    "translation": "QUERY LENGTH LIMIT EXCEEDED. MAX ALLOWED QUERY : 500 CHARS"
  },
